`DataIntegrityViolationExceptionHandler` maps DB/constraint violations to a ProblemDetail — but note it uses HTTP 404 (NOT_FOUND), not 400. This matters for the telephone feature: if an invalid telephone reaches `SaveOwner` and trips the entity `@Pattern` at persist, whether it surfaces as `DataIntegrityViolationException` (→404 here) vs a 400 determines whether `errorRejectsTooFewDigits` (expects 400) passes.

## Directory structure

`src/main/resources/officefloor/`:
```
officefloor/
  escalation/
    java.lang.Exception.yml
    org.springframework.dao.DataIntegrityViolationException.yml
    org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.MissingOwnerFieldsException.yml
    org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.NotFoundException.yml
    org.springframework.security.authorization.AuthorizationDeniedException.yml
    org.springframework.web.bind.MethodArgumentNotValidException.yml
  rest/
    index.GET.yml
    api/
      owners.GET.yml   owners.POST.yml
      owners/{ownerId}.GET.yml   {ownerId}.PUT.yml   {ownerId}.DELETE.yml
      owners/{ownerId}/pets.POST.yml
      owners/{ownerId}/pets/{petId}.GET.yml   {petId}.PUT.yml
      owners/{ownerId}/pets/{petId}/visits.POST.yml
      pets.GET.yml  pets/{petId}.GET/PUT/DELETE.yml
      pettypes*.yml  specialties*.yml  vets*.yml  visits*.yml  users.POST.yml
      v2/owners.GET.yml  v2/pets.GET.yml
```

Owner-related Java packages:
- `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner` — function steps: `RequireOwnerFields, ValidateOwner, BuildOwner, ApplyOwner, LoadOwner, SaveOwner, DeleteOwner, ListOwners, ListOwnersPage, BuildOwnersPet, LoadOwnersPet, RespondWithOwner, RespondWithOwnerCreated, RespondWithOwnerUpdated`
- `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.model` — `Owner` (extends `Person`)
- `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.mapper` — `OwnerMapper` (MapStruct)
- `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.repository` (+ `jpa`, `jdbc`, `springdatajpa`) — `OwnerRepository` and impls
- `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation` — exception handlers
- `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.dto` — generated DTOs (`OwnerFieldsDto`, `OwnerDto`, ...), only present after a build.

## Key takeaway for implementing telephone-normalize

To satisfy `AcceptanceTest`, normalization (strip all non-digits) + an exact-10-digit check must be added to the POST create pipeline — most naturally inside `RequireOwnerFields` (or a new step before `BuildOwner`), setting the cleaned value back on the DTO so the entity's `@Pattern("^[0-9]{10}$")` is satisfied and the stored/returned `telephone` is the 10-digit form. A too-few-digits input must yield 400 (mind that a persist-time entity violation currently routes through `DataIntegrityViolationExceptionHandler` → 404, so the check should happen before save and throw something handled as 400, e.g. via `MissingOwnerFieldsException`-style handling or the `@Valid`/`MethodArgumentNotValidException` path).

